test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T08:37:07.8187900Z             "body": "Preserves original Playwright MCP tools and adds a bounded local batch/jobs companion. Publishing remains disabled. **Draft; release acceptance BLOCKED; mission incomplete.**\n\nLatest tested source `bea4780d370deec0c36ae64c965dfc24157b385d` (native80): **1,900 reported test passes / 10 failures**. [Batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39739439069):1,446/6; [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39739439372):454/4. Both workflows fail. All17 non-soak jobs conclude; optional soak skips; reported test skips/cancellations0. No separate failed diagnostic JSON controls this round.\n\nAll3 actual Codex clients complete1k with model0/owned0 (Linux38.751s,Windows38.431s,Mac63.971s). All journal lanes112/113, five175-file production installs, strict ownership units5/5, all-action15/15, cancellation15/15 (60 scenarios), HTTP privacy15/15 (120 scenarios), and five supervised20-run integrity fixtures pass. New actual-factory HTTP and live-fork/child guardian capture are natively verified. No production runtime changes since9591621; only seven test source files changed throughbea4780.\n\nRemaining failures: Windows raw concurrent screenshot close timeout (actual factory kill fallback resolves), three raw Firefox input failures across headless/headed/pipe, FF429 lifecycle timeout after2GET/2finished but0navigation acknowledgements, Mac synchronous MCP975 timeout with terminated/removed cleanup; original Mac highlight screenshot protocol error; original Windows ARIA connection closure, prompt and popup timeouts. Mac modal/Windows legacy follow-ups and later scenarios in failed cases are unexecuted. Failed inputs are never replayed. Later private/inherited/protocol/stock10/10 controls are healthy but do not explain failed executions.\n\nThe new Firefox diagnostic records actual public root exit after cleanup on two native input failures; root exit does not prove tree cleanup or input causality. A two-candidate legacy comparison has exact recorded replacement-birth relationships and full rows/lifetime ledgers retained. This does NOT classify native79's136 guardian/142 HTTP audit candidates or older unknowns. Those original snapshots lack sufficient birth data; fresh process tables cannot reconstruct old incarnations. No role/name/age/window exclusion, PID-based signal/lease authority or historical debt clearance.\n\nAll17 native80 ordinary job log reads succeed; source and exact evidence are saved under docs/evidence/worker-ci-eightieth-* and native80-*. The final follow-up contains documentation/evidence only, with runtime/test source unchanged. No repeat test claim is made for documentation. Any automatically triggered documentation CI remains separate from native80 acceptance.\n\n`docs/RELEASE_BLOCKERS.md` records unrecoverable historical evidence, unresolved native failures under unchanged budgets, and unsupported/operator-dependent gates. `docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md` keeps G00–G18 incomplete. No artifact download/auth/TLS bypass, privileged installation, deadline raises, forced/replayed input, default transport/channel switch, merge or publication. This blocker record is not a waiver or successful release acceptance.\n",
